Inclusion Criteria

* Male or female aged 40-75 years at time of screening;
* Availability for longitudinal follow-up;
* Signed informed consent

Specifically for CKD participants:

* CKD stage G3a/G3b, or stage G4-G5 without kidney replacement therapy, or stage G5 undergoing hemodialysis (HD) for more than 3 months;
* MoCA score in the range \[18-25\];41

Specifically for controls:

* Normal renal function:

  * For controls aged \< 65 years, eGFR ≥ 90 mL/min/1.73 m2;
  * For controls aged ≥ 65 years, eGFR ≥ 60 mL/min/1.73 m2.
* No detectable proteinuria at screening (negative urine dipstick);
* MoCA score ≥ 26/30.

Exclusion Criteria

* Contraindication to MRI including claustrophobia, pregnancy or breastfeeding, cardiac pacemakers, aneurysm clips, or other MRI-incompatible devices, or inability to undergo MRI;
* Pre-existing neurological disorders known to affect cognitive function (e.g., dementia, Parkinson's disease, multiple sclerosis, epilepsy or neurodegenerative disorders);
* History of ischemic or hemorrhagic stroke and/or previous brain surgery;
* History of severe traumatic brain injury;
* Treated or untreated clinically significant depressive disorder that, in the investigator's judgment, may interfere with cognitive assessment;
* Recent hospitalization for acute events within the last 3 months, except for percutaneous transluminal angioplasty (PTA) of fistula, catheter replacement and elective hospitalizations;
* Serious acute illness within the last 3 months;
* Active solid tumors with or without metastasis;
* Inflammatory bowel disease;
* Systemic corticosteroid treatment for \> 6 months at a prednisone-equivalent dose \> 10 mg/day;
* Planned pregnancy during the 18-month follow-up period;

Specifically for CKD patients:

* Peritoneal dialysis;
* Kidney transplantation at enrolment;

Specifically for controls:

● Any chronic clinically significant condition, except for hypertension treated with \< 3 antihypertensive drugs.
